The factor tree for $90$ is started below. What is the prime factorisation of $90$ in index form?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\node (a) at (0,2.5) {$90$};
\node (b) at (-1.4,1.5) {$9$};
\node (c) at (1.4,1.5) {$10$};
\node[draw,minimum size=0.5cm] (d) at (-2.2,0.5) {};
\node[draw,minimum size=0.5cm] (e) at (-0.6,0.5) {};
\node[draw,minimum size=0.5cm] (f) at (0.6,0.5) {};
\node[draw,minimum size=0.5cm] (g) at (2.2,0.5) {};
\draw (a)--(b);
\draw (a)--(c);
\draw (b)--(d);
\draw (b)--(e);
\draw (c)--(f);
\draw (c)--(g);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What is wrong with this factor tree for $52$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\node (a) at (0,2.2) {$52$};
\node (b) at (-1.3,1.2) {$4$};
\node (c) at (1.3,1.2) {$13$};
\node (d) at (-2.1,0.2) {$2$};
\node (e) at (-0.5,0.2) {$2$};
\node (f) at (0.5,0.2) {$1$};
\node (g) at (2.1,0.2) {$13$};
\draw (a)--(b);
\draw (a)--(c);
\draw (b)--(d);
\draw (b)--(e);
\draw (c)--(f);
\draw (c)--(g);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$p$ is a prime number and the factor tree below is complete, so every leaf is that same prime. Which number could it be factorising?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\node (a) at (0,2.4) {$?$};
\node (b) at (-1.3,1.4) {$p$};
\node[draw,minimum size=0.5cm] (c) at (1.3,1.4) {};
\node (d) at (0.5,0.4) {$p$};
\node (e) at (2.1,0.4) {$p$};
\draw (a)--(b);
\draw (a)--(c);
\draw (c)--(d);
\draw (c)--(e);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
